# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
# ...except the template. It documents each variable and carries no secrets —
# some entries do have illustrative defaults, so "names only" was never quite
# true. The README tells you to copy it, so it has to be in the repository.
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

public/@powersync

# Playwright MCP tool's own snapshots/screenshots when no output path is
# given — session debugging artifacts, not project source. Also watched by
# `next dev`'s file watcher, so leaving these accumulate triggers a
# recompile storm on every browser_snapshot/console_messages call.
.playwright-mcp/

# Internal development process — kept local, never published.
# These are working notes about how the product was built (session-by-session
# decisions, review findings, what was tried and rejected). They are useful to
# whoever is building, and nobody else's business.
context-sessions/
new-prompt/
README.md

# Specs and implementation plans. Same reasoning as above: they carry pricing
# decisions, security findings, roadmap timing and the arguments behind them.
#
# THIS DOES NOT UNPUBLISH WHAT IS ALREADY PUSHED. Ten spec and plan files were
# committed between 11 and 13 Aug 2026 to a PUBLIC repository, and remain in
# git history for anyone who clones it. Adding a path here only stops future
# files being added; removing the history needs a rewrite (git filter-repo)
# and a force push, or the repository being made private. Same caveat doc 16
# recorded when context-sessions/ was untracked.
docs/superpowers/

# Contains the audit of which advertised features do not actually exist.
docs/product-reference.md

# ── Untracked on 18 Aug 2026 ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ⚠️ LISTING A PATH HERE DOES NOT UNTRACK IT. Everything below was already
# being tracked and had to be removed with `git rm --cached` as well. That is
# exactly how `README.md` above ended up published for weeks while sitting in
# this file: it was ignored and tracked at the same time, and git keeps
# tracking what it already tracks.
#
# blue/ — the previous frontend, kept locally as a reference during the port.
# 198 files and 2.1 MB of it were in the repository, including the Word drafts
# of the privacy policy, terms and cookie policy, an SEO audit, ten
# session-by-session build notes under "context & sessions/", two files under
# docs/superpowers/, a demo seed script and the brand asset archives. Every
# category this file already says is "nobody else's business" was published
# anyway, one directory down.
blue/

# Internal narrative of what changed and why, and it names the deployment host.
WHATS-CHANGED.md

# Playwright's run artifacts.
test-results/

# Machine-local scheduler lock, not project source.
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# The superpowers workspace, if it is ever created at the root.
.superpowers/
